  "statement": "For the hash-pinned A1 production coefficients and A10-A13 strict sharp cubes, all prior A13 reductions remain binding at T4. R-085 proves a nonorthogonal weighted causal Schur theorem: a complete mixed Cartan production atom estimate with exponent s>1/2 would spend the triangular root/input sum once, without pairwise output orthogonality. At s=7/12 and eta=1/12 its exact constant is 572.4472106721531... and its gap factor is 2^(-7C/6), but the production atom estimate is not proved. R-085 also expands the nonlinear rational Pauli--Fierz endpoint exactly into five form-payable unshifted families, one signed shifted-Hessian pair, and one retained positive square. The five families have totals 7/20, 7/10, 13/30, 3/5, and 23/30 and worst required moment 30/7. Third-derivative and rational-only fixtures refute deletion, positivity, and fixed-square Schur shortcuts, but not a coupled form bound. The production atom, coupled rational shifted-Hessian bound, complete signed NEAR, REG, overlap-stable progression, controlled-shell one-use, and q=10/9 Nelson remain open.",
